# Lesson 2, new hand (Mike's texture pair, first hand): a solid minimum opening.
title: A solid minimum: open
id: L02-31
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.1, 2.2
student: S
board: 31
dealer: S
vulnerable: NS

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  Q84    K72    J964   K87
  E  T63    Q84    A32    AT54
  S  AK752  A963   85     62
  W  J9     JT5    KQT7   QJ93

auction:
  S 1S*    = 13+ points, at least four spades
     key: 11 HCP plus 1 for each doubleton is 13. Your high cards are all in your long suits, so this is a solid opening.
     not Pass: Did you count the doubletons? 11 plus 2 is 13, enough to open.
     not *: With 13 points and five spades, what does the lesson say to open?
  W Pass
  N 2S     = 6-9 points and spade support
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: at most 22
     key: Partner showed 6-9. 13 plus 9 is 22 at most, short of the 25 a game needs. Pass.
     not *: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Counting the doubletons you had 13 points, and your aces and kings are
  in your long suits, so this is a solid opening. Partner's raise showed
  6-9 points. Your side has at most 22, so you pass. You are declarer,
  because you bid spades first, and so West will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  trumps out: 5
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W DK  N D4  E D2  S D5
  2   W DQ  N D6  E D3  S D8
  3   W CQ  N C7  E C4  S C2
      note: West switches suits.
  4   W CJ  N CK  E CA  S C6
  5   E S3  S SA  W S9  N S4
      note: East switches to a trump.
  6   S SK  W SJ  N S8  E S6
      note: The plan: draw trumps, then set up your fourth heart. Keep drawing trumps.
  7   S S5  W DT  N SQ  E ST
      note: The last trump, to dummy's queen.
  8   N HK  E H4  S H3  W H5
      note: Now the hearts: the king first, the high card from the short side.
  9   N H2  E H8  S HA  W HT
      note: Over to your ♥A.
  10  S H6  W HJ  N H7  E HQ
      note: Give up a heart. Your last heart will then be a winner.
  11  E DA  S S2  W D7  N D9
  12  S H9  W C3  N C8  E C5
      note: Your last heart is high.
  13  S S7  W C9  N DJ  E CT
      note: 8 tricks: 2♠ made.

play recap:
  The plan: draw trumps, then set up your fourth heart.

  2♠ made. Your aces and kings worked well together, which is what makes a
  minimum opening a solid one.
